From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:12:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Potion effects queued in their walk are applied once; fewer
 objects a tick

CraftBukkit never cleared effectsToProcess: an effect added or removed from inside
the effects' walk (a listener of the event a poison or regeneration tick calls) was
added or removed again every tick after, so a removal queued once took that effect
off for good. The list is cleared after it is applied, and an entity with no effects
skips the walk and its two iterators. Also without allocating: inBlock's position,
the world of a movement packet (getWorldServer walked the world list), the players of
a ticked chunk, and the boss bar's target.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

